From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] PADDUH/PSUBUH: saturate like the PS2

What broke:
  PADDUH became _mm_add_epi16 and PSUBUH _mm_sub_epi16: arithmetic that
  wraps around (0x0001 - 0x0002 = 0xFFFF). On the PS2 they saturate
  (0xFFFF at most, 0 at least). Ben 10 uses PSUBUH 27 times
  (docs/findings/09 s.5).

Why:
  PCSX2 MMI.cpp _PADDUH / _PSUBUH: sum > 0xFFFF -> 0xFFFF; difference <= 0
  -> 0. The 8-bit versions (PADDUB/PSUBUB) already used the saturating SSE
  instructions; the 16-bit ones did not.

The fix:
  _mm_adds_epu16 / _mm_subs_epu16.

How it was found:
  Test PsubuhClampsAtZero; PADDUH found by reading the same table.

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
index a2bcb77..1f801f7 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
@@ -105,9 +105,10 @@ namespace ps2recomp
         case MMI1_PEXTUW:
             return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, PS2_PEXTUW(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));", rd, rs, rt);
         case MMI1_PADDUH:
-            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_add_epi16(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));", rd, rs, rt);
+            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_adds_epu16(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));", rd, rs, rt);
         case MMI1_PSUBUH:
-            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_sub_epi16(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));", rd, rs, rt);
+            // PADDUH/PSUBUH saturate (unsigned) like PADDUB/PSUBUB (PCSX2 MMI.cpp _PADDUH/_PSUBUH).
+            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_subs_epu16(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));", rd, rs, rt);
         case MMI1_PEXTUH:
             return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, PS2_PEXTUH(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));", rd, rs, rt);
         case MMI1_PADDUB:
